@startuml infra-overview

title From git push to a live request hitting the Ingress

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

actor "You (developer)" as Dev

package "GitHub Repository" as Repo {
  folder "terraform/\n  stacks/apps/*.tf\n  environments/<env>/apps/\n    backend.tfvars\n    terraform.tfvars" as TFCode
  folder "k8s/\n  *.yml manifests" as K8sCode
  folder "users_app/, posts_app/, ...\n  each with a Dockerfile" as AppCode
  folder "config.yaml\n(tf_stacks, k8s_manifests, apps)" as Config
}

package "GitHub Environment: student1\n(secrets, NOT in git)" as GHSecrets {
  card "AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID\nAWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\nAWS_SESSION_TOKEN\n(DB_USERNAME / DB_PASSWORD - optional)" as Secrets
}

package "GitHub Actions - ci_entrega2_deploy.yml" as Pipeline {
  card "Job 1: config\nreads config.yaml,\nvalidates required secrets exist" as Job1
  card "Job 2: terraform apply\nfor each stack in tf_stacks (in order)" as Job2
  card "Job 3: build & push images\nfor each app in config.yaml -> ECR" as Job3
  card "Job 4: kubectl apply\nfor each folder in k8s_manifests (in order)" as Job4
}

package "AWS (us-east-1)" as AWS {

  package "Provisioned by Terraform" as TFOutput {
    node "EKS Cluster\n(control plane + worker nodes)" as EKS
    database "RDS\n(shared_db, PostgreSQL 5432)" as RDS
    folder "ECR repositories\n(one per app, empty at first)" as ECR
    card "S3 bucket\n(Terraform remote state)" as TFState
  }

  package "Deployed by kubectl, running inside EKS" as K8sRuntime {
    component "ingress (NGINX)" as Ingress
    component "rf003 / rf004 / rf005\npods + services" as Orchestrators
    component "users / posts / offers /\nroutes / scores\npods + services" as Apps
  }
}

actor "End user" as EndUser

' ---------------- flow ----------------
Dev -down-> Repo : git push
Dev -down-> Pipeline : Run workflow\n(selects environment = student1)

Pipeline -down-> GHSecrets : injects secrets\nas env vars

Job1 -down-> Job2
Job2 -down-> Job3
Job3 -down-> Job4

Job2 ..> TFCode : reads .tf + .tfvars
Job2 -right-> TFState : reads/writes state\n(tracks what already exists)
Job2 ==> EKS : creates/updates
Job2 ==> RDS : creates/updates
Job2 ==> ECR : creates/updates\n(empty repos)

Job3 ..> AppCode : docker build\n(per Dockerfile)
Job3 ==> ECR : docker push\n(image_name:image_tag)

Job4 ..> K8sCode : reads *.yml
Job4 ==> EKS : kubectl apply\n(talks to K8s API,\nnot AWS API)
EKS -down-> K8sRuntime : schedules pods,\npulls images from ECR

Apps -up-> RDS : each app's own\nschema, port 5432

EndUser -right-> Ingress : HTTPS request
Ingress -down-> Orchestrators : routes by path\n(/rf003/*, /rf004/*, /rf005/*)
Ingress -down-> Apps : routes by path\n(/users/*, /posts/*, ...)

note bottom of Job2
  Terraform only knows about AWS
  resources (EKS cluster itself,
  RDS, ECR, IAM, networking).
  It has no concept of "Pod" or
  "Deployment" - those are
  Kubernetes objects, created
  in a separate step (Job 4).
end note

note bottom of Job4
  kubectl talks to the Kubernetes
  API of the EKS cluster that
  Terraform already created.
  This is a different API/tool
  than Terraform, even though
  both run in the same pipeline.
end note

note right of GHSecrets
  Never committed to git.
  Only exist as GitHub
  Environment secrets, injected
  into the pipeline at runtime.
end note

@enduml
